I suppose you could just do the serialization using  
writeLong(doubleToLongBits()) - maybe it's worth checking the  
difference in efficiency since that would seem like a more reliable  
and clean implementation (it would preserve any custom NaN and the  
stream would be truly just the payload). The only drawback would be if  
Java performs some array serialization optimizations that it could be  
slower.

Cheers,
