In-Reply-To: <4A659D21.9050500@dbmail.com>
References: <4A64683A.7090608@dbmail.com> <4A646FAE.4000403@dbmail.com> <E7C68D37-58FA-42D6-B4AF-80F800F8469F@r-project.org> <4A658181.4040900@dbmail.com> <4A659D21.9050500@dbmail.com>
Message-ID: <4A86F56C.5020003@dbmail.com>


Hi,

Sorry to get back at this thread after some time, but I just realized 
that the wrap method could also be used in assign, so that we could 
replace the many assign methods by something like this :


	/**
	 * Convenience method to assign in the global environment. This first 
wraps
	 * o into a REXP object and then assign it to the symbol.
	 *
	 * @param symbol name of the object in the R session
	 * @param o object to assign to the symbol
  	 */
	public void assign( String symbol, Object o ) throws REngineException {
		REXP rx = wrap( o ) ;
		if( rx == null){
			throw new REngineException( this, "Could not convert object to REXP" ) ;
		} else{
			assign(symbol, rx, null);
		}
	}
	
Romain


