The idiom I usually use is this ;

int key = r.lock(); // r is an instance of JRIEngine
try{
	// some code that involves parseAndEval, ...
} catch( Exception e ){
} finally{
	r.unlock( key );
}

A syntax error in R should generate a REngineException with the message 
"Parse Error", ... well if you patched JRIEngine with the patch in this 
thread: http://thread.gmane.org/gmane.comp.lang.r.rosuda.devel/893

Does that help ?

